WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.940
- In the last weeks, and months,
we interviewed candidates

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.900
for different roles in our company.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.936
And it was just insane to see and observe

00:00:07.936 --> 00:00:12.270
what some of these people do
and say in these interviews.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:16.940
In this video I'm covering
four tips for crucial mistakes

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.400
which I have observed other
people to do quite frequently

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.580
in these kind of job interviews,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.770
and I'd like to discuss
them to help you avoid

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.840
these mistakes when you are
interviewing for new roles.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.650
Hi guys, my name is Heinrich,

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:32.220
welcome to another coffee
break with Firm Learning.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.410
I hope you're having all a great day.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.440
Today I was sitting, again and still,

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.280
at my home office here in Munich,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.680
and while I was working
on different tasks,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.560
I was reflecting a bit on
the last weeks and months.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.300
Because in our company,
and as some of you know,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.665
I left consulting,
about a half a year ago,

00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:52.700
and now I joined a retail
company in Germany,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.260
and I have a CTO role in this company.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.610
So in our company, in the
last weeks and months,

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.960
we interviewed different
candidates for several roles,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.700
and now reflecting on that,
it was just crazy, right?!

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.220
So, while we had some amazing candidates,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.970
that really fit the roles well,

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:13.910
we had also some candidates
which did or said things

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:17.370
which I just cannot believe
that these people said that.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.800
So reflected a bit on that,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.260
and I tried to come up with a
bit of a condensate of that,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.285
so what were the top four mistakes

00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:26.900
that these people were
doing in the interview.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.000
And apparently, these
people didn't realize

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.530
that these were things which probably

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.700
didn't come across very well,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.350
because otherwise they
wouldn't have done it.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.940
And I want to help you
to avoid these mistakes,

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.130
that you do not do these mistakes.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.950
If this is the first time that
you're watching my channel,

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.030
just let me briefly
introduce myself to you.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.290
My name is Heinrich, and on this channel

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.290
I try to help you be successful

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.630
in the first years of your career.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.080
So it doesn't matter if you're
a fresh college graduate,

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:56.010
or you're already in the
first years of your career,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.110
this channel is all about tips and tricks,

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.820
what you can do to help
you become a professional,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.830
and develop yourself
both from the private,

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.440
but also from the work perspective.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.150
So if you like any of the
content on this channel at all,

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.000
please press the like button
for the YouTube algorithm,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.096
and also subscribe to my channel below

00:02:12.096 --> 00:02:14.310
in order that you get all the new videos

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.370
