00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.220
And of course also please
hit the notification bell

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.780
to make sure you're not missing out.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.330
So, four crucial mistakes
that I have observed

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.000
these job candidates do.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.420
Let's start with the first one.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.050
So, this is a lack of
commitment and investment

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.891
from the side of the candidate.

00:02:30.891 --> 00:02:33.330
So what exactly do I mean by that?

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.980
What I mean is that if
you talk to the candidate,

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:37.420
if you interview them,

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.560
there are just some people where you know,

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.370
you just directly sense,

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.524
that you are just one of
many companies on his list,

00:02:44.524 --> 00:02:47.750
that probably is interviewing
with three or four companies

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.920
at the same time, and in the end

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.984
he doesn't really, really
care where exactly he works.

00:02:52.984 --> 00:02:55.340
There are no really hard reasons

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.060
why he would prefer your
company over the other.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.610
And in the end, probably the only thing

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.780
that would matter to him
is either the salary,

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.400
or maybe some other benefits.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.037
But he does not really
care for your company.

00:03:06.037 --> 00:03:09.740
And this especially becomes
obvious when you realize

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.031
that he didn't do any
basic research at all

00:03:13.031 --> 00:03:14.670
about your company.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.125
The bare minimum that you need to prepare

00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:19.940
if you interview for a
company is to at least have

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.890
some basic stats of the
company in your head.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.790
So, what is roughly the revenue
that the company is making?

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.070
How many employees do they have?

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.350
In what geographies do they operate?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.270
So this is the bare minimum of research

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.190
and commitment that you need to show

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.730
in order for us as interviewers,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.630
to make it clear that
you really want the job.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.190
And of course, this is especially easy

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:45.070
if you work for a publicly traded company,

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:48.410
because for these companies
there are annual reports

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.920
that you can just flip through

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.460
and you will easily get
all of these key stats.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.486
But even if it's not a
publicly traded company,

00:03:55.486 --> 00:03:57.630
there are many other sources

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.570
of information that you can use.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.050
So of course, on the one end side,

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.210
you could just look for
the company website,

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.840
or infos on there,

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.700
but even if the company
doesn't have such a website,

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.210
or doesn't provide these
kinds of information on it,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.920
in most countries there is some type

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.800
of commercial registers,
where you can just pull

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.120
these kind of information.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.720
In Germany, there's the handelsregister,

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.810
you can just look into Bundesanzeiger DE,

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.310
it's a publicly available
internet site in Germany.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.580
And then you just type in
the name of the company,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.760
and the latest annual
reports that are filed

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.100
from this company will be available there.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.060
So even if it's not a
publicly traded company,

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.230
but an entity, or an LLC,

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:38.010
or in Germany, a GmbH,

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.302
you will get these kind of
basic financial information

00:04:41.302 --> 00:04:42.630
on the company.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.190
And of course, this might give you also

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.590
important insights as a recruit.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.840
From my perspective, it
would seem very important,

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.390
if you look into joining a company,

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.890
to understand what the financial situation

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.530
is in which the company is in.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:55.907
Is it doing well?

00:04:55.907 --> 00:04:56.930
Is it not doing well?

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.620
If it's not doing really
well, what are the reasons?

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.890
Why is it not doing well?

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.580
How does this might affect your position

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.900
that you want to start in?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.420
So do this basic research,

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.620
and then show your interviewer
that you did this research,

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.890
to give both sides some kind of comfort.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.090
Now, talking about some positive examples,

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.130
what can you actually do in order

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.590
to really show some commitment

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.040
and investment into the company?

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.930
So what one of the
candidates, for instance,

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:23.740
did that we interviewed
is he visited several

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.500
of our stores, and he also made an order

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:30.200
in our online shop, to get a
feel of what the experience is

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.400
when buying with us,
both online and offline.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.280
And he was able to, in the interview,

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.020
give us quite a few
tangible feedback points,

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.780
on what his experience are,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.390
and what he would potentially
recommend to improve.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.690
And as he was also looking to
work in a sales related role,

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.430
of course, this made perfect sense.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.270
And this showed us that
this guy is serious.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.830
I mean, he already did some effort

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.870
to understand what he could improve.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.720
He already showed us
that he has the stamina

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.290
to really go there, do some test orders,

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:58.870
or just go out, visit stores,

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.910
and this already put him far ahead

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.290
of some other applicants
who did not even research

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.490
the most basic information on our company.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:10.300
So do some research, invest
prior to coming to the interview

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.890
in terms of money, or
time, to show the people

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.910
that you are serious, that
you really want the job,

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.380
and are willing to go an
extra mile to get there,

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:20.833
and to provide and add
value for the company.

00:06:24.081 --> 00:06:26.930
A second very big, very big mistake,

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.950
a second very big red flag,

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.270
the big mistake that many candidates do

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.490
is to not show any empathy,

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.510
to not show any self-reflection
in these interviews.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:40.060
So very frequently,
interviews will consist

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.280
of some kind of questions of
the type that they ask you

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.680
what the interviewer thought
may be a difficult problem

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.510
that you faced in your professional life,

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.120
a special challenge that you had

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.830
in your professional life before.

00:06:50.830 --> 00:06:53.040
Just to get a feel of
what type of challenges

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.210
you were already confronted
with in the past.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:58.810
And then also how you react
in these kinds of situations.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.180
And I get the feeling
that some candidates think

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.760
they should avoid at all costs

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:07.165
showing any kind of
weakness, any kind of doubt,

00:07:07.165 --> 00:07:09.460
when answering these kinds of questions.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.720
But this often leads to an
answer that sounds like this,

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.217
with the candidate pretty much saying,

00:07:14.217 --> 00:07:17.157
"That there were these
tough and serious issues

00:07:17.157 --> 00:07:19.767
"that I was facing, and all
these other people around me,

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.627
"they were clueless, they had no idea.

00:07:22.627 --> 00:07:24.377
"They were idiots."
right?

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.027
"But I am then the big hero,

00:07:26.027 --> 00:07:28.527
"and I walked in and I solved everything,

00:07:28.527 --> 00:07:30.920
"and I came up with this great solution."

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:35.630
And the reason why these
kind of answers do not work,

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.130
or are not good answers,

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:41.290
is because they do not
show that you have empathy.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:44.650
They do not show that
you have self-reflection.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.760
That you can put yourself into
the shoes of your colleagues,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:50.750
of other partners, and understand
what they are thinking,

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.490
what they're emotions are.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.920
Because the truth is,
especially when facing tough

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.310
and challenging problems,
it's not black and white.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.980
Some other people might behave

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.080
very counterintuitive to you,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.330
it might be very difficult
for you to understand

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.900
why they are behaving in a certain way.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:08.460
But if you try to put
yourself in their shoes,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.590
and try to understand
what they are feeling,

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.420
what they are thinking,

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.650
then this often enables you to understand

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.966
their perspective, and then
also jointly collaborate

00:08:18.966 --> 00:08:21.540
on at solution to a certain problem.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.090
And these kind of team
oriented problem-solving skills

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.480
are highly important in a lot
of modern work environments.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.420
And the reason why this is so important,

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:34.610
is that today leaders
need to have empathy.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:37.250
It is really difficult to build followers

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.083
in an organization,

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:41.800
to build a tribe of people
that really supports you,

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.270
if you do not have empathy.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.120
If you are not able as a
leader to also help them,

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.610
encourage them, enable them,

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:52.110
and all of this requires
empathy and self-reflection.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.480
And make sure that in
your answers to these kind

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.980
of challenge oriented, or
problem oriented questions,

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:00.430
you show that you have this empathy.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:02.390
This is just so important.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:05.930
A third big mistake that
many people are doing,

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:08.510
is bad-mouthing their old employer.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:10.660
And I get it, it's okay, right?

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:13.750
There's often a reason
why you left your old job,

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.030
maybe you quit the position,

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:17.170
or maybe your employer quit you.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.890
And often this can leave
you with some bad feelings.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.480
And of course, if asked,
it's completely fine

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.130
to maybe also mention a few points

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.800
where you disliked your prior role,

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.720
and what motivated you now
to make the transition.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.900
This is, of course, absolutely fine.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.420
No problem about that.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.820
But then we had some candidates,

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.085
and not only one, but several of them,

00:09:36.085 --> 00:09:39.370
went just on, and on, and on,

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.143
just talking bad about
their prior situation,

00:09:42.143 --> 00:09:45.000
how all of their colleagues,
all of these other people,

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.790
just didn't get it, making
it sound like they were

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.540
pretty much the only
intelligent person in the room.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.960
Describing all kinds of problems
at their prior employer,

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.130
and how they were the
ones who realized it,

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.110
but apparently everybody else around them

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.470
did not realize it.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:03.510
And this type of behavior
is bad for two reasons.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:06.730
First, it just makes you look
like a very negative person.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.970
If I'm looking for
colleagues to work with,

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:10.520
I do not want to have a colleague

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:12.630
who is just complaining about everybody

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.047
and everything all day long.

00:10:14.047 --> 00:10:16.380
I want some positivity around me.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.070
And of course it's okay to also
make some critical remarks,

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.150
but this always needs to be in a context,

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:24.360
and not just out of a habit
of complaining all the time.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.660
So this is the first reason,

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.280
but the second reason comes back

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.010
to another video that I did,

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:32.480
it's called the video "Problem
Solver, Problem Talker".

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.418
And I will include it above me,

00:10:34.418 --> 00:10:37.210
that you can check it out
if you haven't seen it yet,

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:38.870
but it describes how a person

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:43.340
can either be a problem
talker, or a problem solver.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:45.911
And I do not want to go into
all the details right now,

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:48.410
but if you are a person
that just complains,

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.450
or makes it looks like
you've got it all right,

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:51.283
you understood it all,

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:53.760
but just all these other
people around you didn't,

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.500
this very much makes you
look like a problem talker.

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.350
And for reasons I explained
in this other video,

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:04.180
what companies need and
want are problem solvers.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.700
Because the truth is, the
likelihood is pretty high,

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.770
that all the problems
that you are describing

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.730
about your old employer,

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.570
there's a high chance
that you would have had

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.770
some opportunity to do
something about them.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.890
So if all these things were going wrong,

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:21.950
what was your contribution
in your old company

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.920
to fix it, to make it better?

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:26.510
And again, the truth is
usually much more complex

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.630
then you being the intelligent
star who understood it all,

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.620
and wanted to do your best,
but you just couldn't.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.470
Show that you solved these problems,

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:35.450
and then tried your best
to really add value,

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:38.310
and make an impact, and don't
just explain all day long

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.140
about what other peoples are doing wrong.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:42.770
And my last mistake is
regarding body language,

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.830
and perceived energy level.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.740
It is just important to understand

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.470
that how you are perceived as a candidate

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:53.610
is of course driven on the
one hand side by what you say,

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.760
but also, on the other
side, how you say it.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.210
What your body language
is when you say it.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.717
And just let me try to imitate it.

00:12:01.717 --> 00:12:04.090
There were job candidates who were

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:06.290
just making themselves small,

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:10.250
who were sitting like
this in their chairs,

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.720
and some of them said some
really intelligent things.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.190
But if you just say it by talking

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:20.040
in a very monotonous voice,

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:22.730
by talking with a very quiet voice,

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:25.976
if you just make yourself small like this,

00:12:25.976 --> 00:12:30.110
this is just not how
you are perceived well.

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:31.770
It might be all right what you say,

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.410
it might make total sense,

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.360
but you seem like a person who cannot

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:37.230
articulate yourself well,

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.020
who probably has a problem with being

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.390
perceived with some kind of authority

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:42.640
in front of other people.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:44.900
Who would probably have a hard time

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.930
persuading other colleagues,

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.300
which is of course an
important business skill.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:52.880
And also is then perceived
with a low energy level.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.520
And of course, this always comes down

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.120
to personality as well,

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.240
there are some people just naturally have

00:12:58.240 --> 00:12:59.830
a higher energy level than others,

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:01.830
and this is completely fine.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.207
But what usually do
not want as an employer

00:13:04.207 --> 00:13:06.290
to have somebody on an extreme,

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.950
who just sits there, makes themself small,

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:13.230
and just radiates a very low energy level.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.210
What you actually want as an employer

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.030
is somebody who just walks
there with lots of energy,

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:19.746
somebody who looks like he can tackle

00:13:19.746 --> 00:13:21.990
10 new problems every day,

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.877
and can just move mountains, right?

00:13:23.877 --> 00:13:26.510
And of course now I'm exaggerating a bit,

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:29.370
but this is what you're
looking out for as an employer.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.120
So at least try to make
your best impression

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.340
in the job interview.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.660
And even if you are a bit of an introvert,

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.210
this is completely okay, of course,

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.840
so no problem with that,

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.800
but try to at least show some
personality in the interview.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.900
Show that you have some energy in you,

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:48.160
that you can move things, that
you are a mover and shaker,

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.690
so that you'll help your
potential future employer

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:52.790
see this kind of energy in you,

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:55.720
and see this ability of yours
to really tackle things,

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.210
go in there, and also go
into a fight, if required.

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.130
So these were the four mistakes.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.200
So let me just reiterate, and repeat.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.500
So the first is, not showing any kind

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.030
of commitment and investment.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.870
Not showing some kind of
research that you did.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.830
What you need to do is show
that you researched the company,

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.250
that you know the details,

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.230
that you maybe went the extra mile.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:20.630
Maybe called the hotline
in the B2B company,

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.340
looked into a sales demo
to understand the product.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.520
Maybe did a test order

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.560
of whatever the product
is of your company.

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:28.130
Show that you did an investment,

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.290
that you really want to
work for the company,

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:32.190
and add some value for the company.

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.720
Second, especially for leadership roles,

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:38.630
show that you have empathy and
the ability to self reflect.

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:41.370
Portray yourself as a leader
who tries to make an effort

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:44.561
to understand what other
people think and feel.

00:14:44.561 --> 00:14:47.560
Because if you cannot do
that you will struggle.

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.190
And this is something that many
employers will look out for.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:53.410
Third, don't express too much negativity.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.180
Don't go on and on
criticizing your old employer,

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:59.180
just talking how bad everything was,

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.230
and how other people just didn't get it.

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.050
Show some positivity.

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:04.960
People do not want to be surrounded

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.760
by negativity all day long,

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.550
so don't be perceived
as a negative person.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.220
And last but not least, look
out for your body language

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.810
and your perceived energy level.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.740
Show that you have the energy
to tackle difficult tasks,

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.150
and don't make yourself
smaller than you are.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:22.100
And don't talk with a
quiet and monotonous voice,

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.980
because this usually will not help you.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.220
What I can just tell you,

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.670
now having interviewed several candidates

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:28.370
in the last weeks and months,

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.760
if you will do all these things,

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.470
in your next job interview,

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:35.319
I can promise you that you
are a significant step ahead

00:15:35.319 --> 00:15:38.330
of many, many other job
candidates out there.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.830
So, I hope this makes sense to you.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:42.030
Let me know what you
think in the comments,

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:44.890
what are your tips and
tricks for job interviews?

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:47.360
What were situations that
